  {
   "id": 631744,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p dir=\"ltr\">The graph models the height, in feet, of a kickball over time. When is the ball at its maximum height?</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><img alt=\"GRAPH THAT SHOWS THE HEIGHT OF A KICKBALL IN FEET AS A FUNCTION OF TIME. THE FUNCTION IS MODELED BY AN UPSIDE DOWN PARABOLA WITH A \\(y\\)-intercepts OF 0, \\(x\\)-intercepts OF 0 AND 5, AND MAXIMUM AT THE POINT (2.5, 31).  \" src=\"exercises/media/8835d87d3760dbe1.jpg\" width=\"300\"><br></p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1222586,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"h(2.5) = 31\">h(2.5) = 31</span>; The maximum height is about 2.5 feet. It occurred about 31 seconds after the ball was kicked."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222585,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"h(1)=20\">h(1)=20</span>; The maximum height occurred 1 second after the ball was kicked."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222584,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"h(5)=0\">h(5)=0</span>; The maximum height occurs about 6 seconds after the ball was kicked."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222587,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"h(2.5) = 31\">h(2.5) = 31</span>; The maximum height is about 31 feet. It occurred about 2.5 seconds after the ball was kicked."
    }
